{"id":"eee858dbcfa90e95","group":"68","path":"68/68-thm-hypersimple-implies-simple.md","title":"Hypersimple Sets Are Simple","display":"thm-hypersimple-implies-simple — Hypersimple Sets Are Simple","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)","book_abbrev":"68","label":"68-thm-hypersimple-implies-simple","aliases":["68-thm-hypersimple-implies-simple"],"display":"thm-hypersimple-implies-simple — Hypersimple Sets Are Simple","depends_on":["[[68-df-hypersimple-set]]","[[68-df-simple-set]]"],"source_edition":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF","source_location":"17.3 p.64 / PDF 73","verification_status":"proved-in-note","source_proof_status":"source-proof-and-local-proof-reviewed"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"68"},{"key":"label","html":"68-thm-hypersimple-implies-simple"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>68-thm-hypersimple-implies-simple</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-hypersimple-implies-simple — Hypersimple Sets Are Simple"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"24aa74ef95a06c55\" href=\"?note=24aa74ef95a06c55\" title=\"68-df-hypersimple-set\">68-df-hypersimple-set</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"c1ec7730895203eb\" href=\"?note=c1ec7730895203eb\" title=\"68-df-simple-set\">68-df-simple-set</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF"},{"key":"source_location","html":"17.3 p.64 / PDF 73"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"proved-in-note"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"source-proof-and-local-proof-reviewed"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\subseteq\\mathbb N\">\\(A\\subseteq\\mathbb N\\)</span>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HyperSimple}\">\\(\\mathrm{HyperSimple}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"24aa74ef95a06c55\" href=\"?note=24aa74ef95a06c55\" title=\"68-df-hypersimple-set\">68-df-hypersimple-set</a>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Simple}\">\\(\\mathrm{Simple}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"c1ec7730895203eb\" href=\"?note=c1ec7730895203eb\" title=\"68-df-simple-set\">68-df-simple-set</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HyperSimple}(A)\\Rightarrow\\mathrm{Simple}(A).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{HyperSimple}(A)\\Rightarrow\\mathrm{Simple}(A).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>对应原书 17.3，印刷 p.64 / PDF p.73，陈述与证明均已比对。反证：若补集含无限 RE 子集 B，对每个 x 同时枚举 B 直到发现 y&gt;x，令 g(x)=y。无限性使此搜索总终止，故 g 是全递归函数。取 F(x)=g(x)+1，就有 x&lt;g(x)&lt;F(x) 且 g(x)∉A，违背超简单定义。加 1 是为保持原书严格上界；不能仅用 g(x) 作为同一严格上界。</p>\n<p>创建前搜索本书原子和目录，已有超简单/简单定义及简单集存在性，但无 17.3 对应原子；新增本节点补齐实际书中蕴涵链，不复用其他书同名概念。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"68-df-hypersimple-set","status":"resolved","id":"24aa74ef95a06c55","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[68-df-hypersimple-set]]","embed":false},{"target":"68-df-simple-set","status":"resolved","id":"c1ec7730895203eb","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[68-df-simple-set]]","embed":false},{"target":"68-df-hypersimple-set","status":"resolved","id":"24aa74ef95a06c55","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$A\\subseteq\\mathbb N$。$\\mathrm{HyperSimple}$ 见 [[68-df-hypersimple-set]]，$\\mathrm{Simple}$ 见 [[68-df-simple-set]]。","embed":false},{"target":"68-df-simple-set","status":"resolved","id":"c1ec7730895203eb","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$A\\subseteq\\mathbb N$。$\\mathrm{HyperSimple}$ 见 [[68-df-hypersimple-set]]，$\\mathrm{Simple}$ 见 [[68-df-simple-set]]。","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A\\subseteq\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HyperSimple}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Simple}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HyperSimple}(A)\\Rightarrow\\mathrm{Simple}(A).","display":true}],"bytes":1410,"backlinks":[{"id":"be41c4d7dd143cb1","anchor":"ref-126","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[68-thm-hypersimple-implies-simple]] — theorem"},{"id":"3cb8c24064050ea6","anchor":"ref-173","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[68-thm-hypersimple-implies-simple|thm-hypersimple-implies-simple — Hypersimple Sets Are Simple]]"}],"outgoing":["24aa74ef95a06c55","c1ec7730895203eb"]}